WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.364 --> 00:00:01.625
Miles pulled Edward away from City Hall.

2
00:00:01.665 --> 00:00:08.268
Heading toward the river, they heard the same news being passed from one person to another.

3
00:00:08.288 --> 00:00:09.429
"Have you heard?

4
00:00:09.449 --> 00:00:09.849
The king is dead!"

5
00:00:12.431 --> 00:00:31.397
The words made Edward shudder, and tears came to his eyes.

6
00:00:32.457 --> 00:00:36.579
The man who had been such a tyrant to others had always been gentle with him.

7
00:00:36.599 --> 00:00:43.122
"The country has lost a king, but I have lost a father."

8
00:00:44.322 --> 00:00:46.323
Edward wiped away a tear with his hand.

9
00:00:47.784 --> 00:00:50.965
Miles patted Edward on the back while encouraging him to hurry.

10
00:00:50.985 --> 00:00:55.067
"Long live the king!"

11
00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:57.668
a man shouted as they stepped onto the bridge.

12
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.062
"Long live King Edward!"

13
00:01:01.622 --> 00:01:02.362
others shouted.

14
00:01:02.382 --> 00:01:04.524
"That's me!"

15
00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:05.605
Edward said.

16
00:01:05.625 --> 00:01:09.907
"How strange and wonderful it seems at the same time!"

17
00:01:12.609 --> 00:01:13.470
Miles frowned.

18
00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:17.412
"Something is wrong with this boy," he thought.

19
00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:20.034
"He believes he's the king."

20
00:01:23.076 --> 00:01:26.118
Miles decided to go along with the pauper's fantasy for now.

21
00:01:26.138 --> 00:01:28.300
"Yes, Your Highness."

22
00:01:31.292 --> 00:01:34.555
Edward stopped walking and waited for Miles to stop and turn around.

23
00:01:34.575 --> 00:01:43.562
"Actually, now that I'm king," Edward said, "you should address me as 'Your Majesty' or 'sir.'

24
00:01:44.823 --> 00:01:46.424
By the way, where are we going?"

25
00:01:49.387 --> 00:01:51.449
Miles walked back to where Edward was standing.

26
00:01:51.469 --> 00:01:55.372
"To an inn on the other side of the bridge.

27
00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:01.101
Then after a meal and a good night's sleep, we'll head to Hendon Hall, my family's home in

28
00:02:01.141 --> 00:02:01.661
the country.

29
00:02:02.802 --> 00:02:04.382
You'll be safe there, Your Majesty."

30
00:02:04.402 --> 00:02:13.925
"I'd prefer to go to the palace and—" "So," a voice growled suddenly, "you finally decided to show

31
00:02:14.165 --> 00:02:18.466
up!" John Canty reached out a hand to seize Edward.

32
00:02:19.526 --> 00:02:21.187
"You won't escape again!

33
00:02:21.547 --> 00:02:25.128
If you do, I'll—" Miles stepped between them.

34
00:02:26.108 --> 00:02:27.648
"Not so fast, my friend.

35
00:02:28.969 --> 00:02:31.470
You don't need to be so hard on the boy.

36
00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.670
And why are you bothering him anyway?"

37
00:02:36.251 --> 00:02:38.491
"Not that it's any of your business, but he's my son."

38
00:02:38.511 --> 00:02:40.712
"You're lying!"

39
00:02:41.792 --> 00:02:44.113
Edward peered around Miles to glare at John.

40
00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:48.874
"I hate you, and I'd rather die than go anywhere with you!"

41
00:02:48.894 --> 00:02:52.935
"Then it's settled," Miles said.

42
00:02:52.955 --> 00:02:54.916
"The boy stays with me."

43
00:02:56.896 --> 00:02:58.177
"We'll see about that!"

44
00:02:59.158 --> 00:03:01.500
John tried to push past Miles to reach Edward.

45
00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.404
But Miles raised one arm to block John and put his other hand on his sword.

46
00:03:06.424 --> 00:03:10.207
"Don't even think of touching this lad!"

47
00:03:10.627 --> 00:03:11.388
Miles warned.

48
00:03:11.408 --> 00:03:14.891
"I just saved him from being thrown in the river.

49
00:03:16.392 --> 00:03:19.174
I'm not going to let you do something worse to him!"

50
00:03:20.695 --> 00:03:23.738
For a moment John looked like he might challenge Miles.

51
00:03:25.739 --> 00:03:28.982
But then, muttering curses and threats, he moved away.

52
00:03:29.002 --> 00:03:33.186
"Phew! That was close!"

53
00:03:33.706 --> 00:03:34.326
Edward said.

54
00:03:34.346 --> 00:03:38.250
"That man keeps mistaking me for his son."

55
00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:43.774
"Don't worry, Your Majesty," Miles said as they crossed the bridge.

56
00:03:43.794 --> 00:03:48.858
"I vow to protect you from all danger and nurse you back to health.

57
00:03:50.459 --> 00:03:52.381
Think of me as your older brother."

58
00:03:53.682 --> 00:03:57.240
"Thank you for your protection, but I'm not sick," Edward said.

59
00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:02.322
"And if you were my older brother, you'd be king instead of me."

60
00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:07.425
"I guess that's right," Miles said slowly.

61
00:04:07.445 --> 00:04:12.827
"Well, here we are at the inn where I'm staying."

62
00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:18.189
Miles ordered some hot food to be sent to his room on the top floor.

63
00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.151
Their meal soon arrived.

64
00:04:22.171 --> 00:04:25.492
"We'll have a regular feast."

65
00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:29.114
Miles rubbed his hands together in anticipation.

66
00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:35.000
"It may not be as fine as the mayor's banquet, but—" He was stopped by the sight of

67
00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:36.942
Edward standing at the wash basin.

68
00:04:36.962 --> 00:04:40.446
"What are you waiting for, lad?"

69
00:04:40.466 --> 00:04:44.369
"I want to wash my hands and face."

70
00:04:44.389 --> 00:04:48.013
"Oh, is that all?

71
00:04:49.194 --> 00:04:50.916
You don't need my permission to do that."

72
00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:56.673
Edward remained motionless, except for impatiently tapping his foot.

73
00:04:56.693 --> 00:04:59.554
"What's the problem?"

74
00:05:00.074 --> 00:05:00.794
Miles said.

75
00:05:00.814 --> 00:05:03.815
"The water and the towel are right there."

76
00:05:03.835 --> 00:05:09.297
"Please stop talking and pour the water into the basin," Edward said.

77
00:05:11.638 --> 00:05:15.539
Trying not to laugh, Miles picked up the pitcher and did as he was told.

78
00:05:15.559 --> 00:05:19.660
"My goodness," Miles thought.

79
00:05:21.208 --> 00:05:24.029
"He's acting like he really is a member of the royal family."

80
00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:30.091
I need to dry myself."

81
00:05:31.851 --> 00:05:35.612
Edward raised an eyebrow, indicating the towel that was right in front of him.

82
00:05:38.473 --> 00:05:40.414
Miles obediently handed him the towel.

83
00:05:43.655 --> 00:05:46.976
While Miles washed his own face and hands, Edward sat at the table.

84
00:05:49.264 --> 00:05:52.187
Miles pulled out the other chair and prepared to join him.

85
00:05:52.207 --> 00:05:54.949
"What are you doing?"

86
00:05:55.349 --> 00:05:56.030
Edward cried.

87
00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.072
"I'm sitting!

88
00:05:58.492 --> 00:06:03.376
And no one else sits while the king is sitting—not without the king's permission.

89
00:06:04.638 --> 00:06:06.399
Your role is to serve me."

90
00:06:06.419 --> 00:06:10.122
"Yes, Your Highness.

91
00:06:10.302 --> 00:06:10.903
Forgive me."

92
00:06:13.065 --> 00:06:16.328
Amused, Miles stood obediently behind Edward's chair.

93
00:06:18.792 --> 00:06:21.835
As Edward ate, he relaxed and became more friendly.

94
00:06:21.855 --> 00:06:25.577
"I think you said that your name is Miles Hendon?"

95
00:06:26.898 --> 00:06:28.099
Edward put down his fork.

96
00:06:28.119 --> 00:06:31.382
"I'd like to know more about you.

97
00:06:32.363 --> 00:06:33.744
Please tell me your story."
